### ClearWood Furnitures — Prompt 5: admin catalog
### VS Code REST Client. Runs top to bottom; @variables carry state forward.

@host = http://localhost:7180
@api = {{host}}/api/v1

### 1. Sign in (sets cw_adm_at / cw_adm_rt / cw_adm_csrf)
# @name adminLogin
POST {{api}}/admin/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "admin@clearwood.local",
  "password": "ChangeMe@12345"
}

###
@csrf = {{adminLogin.response.headers.$['set-cookie'][2]}}

### 2. The admin tree (inactive rows included)
# @name tree
GET {{api}}/admin/catalog/categories/tree

### Pick the "Sofas" root from the tree response.
@sofasId = {{tree.response.body.data.0.id}}

### 3. Create "Recliner Sofas" under Sofas
# @name newCategory
POST {{api}}/admin/catalog/categories
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF-Token: {{csrf}}

{
  "name": "Recliner Sofas",
  "parentId": "{{sofasId}}",
  "kind": "STANDARD",
  "showInMenu": true,
  "shortDescription": "Motorised and manual recliners in fabric and leather."
}

###
@categoryId = {{newCategory.response.body.data.id}}
@categoryVersion = {{newCategory.response.body.data.version}}

### 4. The public tree reflects it immediately — no restart, no cache flush
GET {{api}}/catalog/categories/tree

### 5. Rename it. `version` is mandatory: a stale value returns 409 STALE_RESOURCE.
PATCH {{api}}/admin/catalog/categories/{{categoryId}}
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF-Token: {{csrf}}

{ "name": "Recliner Sofas & Loungers", "version": {{categoryVersion}} }

### 6. Re-sending the SAME version now fails — proof of optimistic locking
PATCH {{api}}/admin/catalog/categories/{{categoryId}}
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF-Token: {{csrf}}

{ "name": "Should not apply", "version": {{categoryVersion}} }

### 7. Any slug change left a 301 behind
GET {{api}}/admin/catalog/categories/{{categoryId}}/redirects

### 8. Move it (path and depth are recomputed for the whole subtree)
POST {{api}}/admin/catalog/categories/{{categoryId}}/move
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF-Token: {{csrf}}

{ "parentId": null, "position": 0, "version": 1 }

### 9. Reorder siblings
POST {{api}}/admin/catalog/categories/reorder
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF-Token: {{csrf}}

{ "items": [{ "id": "{{categoryId}}", "position": 2 }] }

### 10. What would a delete touch? (children + product counts, before anything happens)
GET {{api}}/admin/catalog/categories/{{categoryId}}/delete-impact?strategy=BLOCK

### 11. Create a product. Idempotency-Key makes a retry safe.
# @name newProduct
POST {{api}}/admin/catalog/products
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF-Token: {{csrf}}
Idempotency-Key: demo-product-0001

{
  "sku": "CW-RECL-001",
  "name": "Aspen Recliner",
  "productType": "VARIABLE",
  "basePricePaise": 4599900,
  "description": "A two-motor recliner with an independent headrest, built on a kiln-dried hardwood frame and upholstered in stain-resistant fabric.",
  "warrantyMonths": 36,
  "lengthMm": 1900,
  "widthMm": 900,
  "heightMm": 1050
}

###
@productId = {{newProduct.response.body.data.id}}
@productVersion = {{newProduct.response.body.data.version}}

### 12. Replaying the same key returns the ORIGINAL response (Idempotent-Replay: true)
POST {{api}}/admin/catalog/products
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF-Token: {{csrf}}
Idempotency-Key: demo-product-0001

{
  "sku": "CW-RECL-001",
  "name": "Aspen Recliner",
  "productType": "VARIABLE",
  "basePricePaise": 4599900
}

### 13. Categories (the parent "All X" bucket is added automatically)
PUT {{api}}/admin/catalog/products/{{productId}}/categories
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF-Token: {{csrf}}

{ "primaryCategoryId": "{{categoryId}}", "categoryIds": [] }

### 14. Preview a variant matrix — nothing is written
### Replace the ids with a variant-defining attribute and its values.
@colourAttributeId = REPLACE_WITH_ATTRIBUTE_ID
# @name matrix
POST {{api}}/admin/catalog/products/{{productId}}/variants/matrix/preview
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF-Token: {{csrf}}

{
  "attributeIds": ["{{colourAttributeId}}"],
  "selectedValueIdsByAttribute": {
    "{{colourAttributeId}}": ["VALUE_ID_1", "VALUE_ID_2", "VALUE_ID_3"]
  },
  "skuPattern": "{PRODUCT_SKU}-{ATTR:COLOUR}-{INDEX}",
  "pricingMode": "INHERIT"
}

### 15. Generate — only the missing combinations are created
POST {{api}}/admin/catalog/products/{{productId}}/variants/matrix/generate
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF-Token: {{csrf}}
Idempotency-Key: demo-matrix-0001

{
  "attributeIds": ["{{colourAttributeId}}"],
  "selectedValueIdsByAttribute": {
    "{{colourAttributeId}}": ["VALUE_ID_1", "VALUE_ID_2", "VALUE_ID_3"]
  },
  "skuPattern": "{PRODUCT_SKU}-{ATTR:COLOUR}-{INDEX}",
  "pricingMode": "INHERIT"
}

### 16. Variants of the product
GET {{api}}/admin/catalog/products/{{productId}}/variants

### 16a. (Prompt 3) A second variant with the same options is refused, in any pair order:
### 409 VARIANT_COMBINATION_EXISTS, details.variantId names the holder.
### A value from another attribute is 422. Concurrent writes may get 409 WRITE_CONFLICT: retry.
POST {{api}}/admin/catalog/products/{{productId}}/variants
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF-Token: {{csrf}}

{
  "sku": "DEMO-DUPLICATE-COMBO",
  "attributeValues": [{ "attributeId": "{{colourAttributeId}}", "attributeValueId": "VALUE_ID_1" }]
}

### 16b. Exactly one default per product: this demotes the previous default atomically
POST {{api}}/admin/catalog/products/{{productId}}/variants/{{variantId}}/set-default
X-CSRF-Token: {{csrf}}

###
@variantId = REPLACE_WITH_VARIANT_ID

### 17. Adjust stock. Every movement writes a ledger row in the same transaction.
POST {{api}}/admin/catalog/variants/{{variantId}}/inventory/adjust
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF-Token: {{csrf}}
Idempotency-Key: demo-stock-0001

{ "delta": 12, "reason": "PURCHASE", "note": "Opening consignment" }

### 18. Concurrency-safe variant: refuse the write unless stock is still what you saw
POST {{api}}/admin/catalog/variants/{{variantId}}/inventory/adjust
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF-Token: {{csrf}}

{ "delta": -3, "expectedBalance": 999, "reason": "CORRECTION" }

### 19. The ledger reads as a running balance
GET {{api}}/admin/catalog/variants/{{variantId}}/inventory?limit=20

### 20. Low stock report
GET {{api}}/admin/catalog/inventory/low-stock?threshold=3

### 21. Try to publish — 422 with every blocker itemised
POST {{api}}/admin/catalog/products/{{productId}}/publish
X-CSRF-Token: {{csrf}}

### 22. Read the blockers without attempting a publish
GET {{api}}/admin/catalog/products/{{productId}}/publish-blockers

### 23. Fix them: tax class, primary image, then publish
PATCH {{api}}/admin/catalog/products/{{productId}}
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF-Token: {{csrf}}

{ "taxClassId": "REPLACE_WITH_TAX_CLASS_ID", "version": {{productVersion}} }

###
POST {{api}}/admin/products/{{productId}}/media
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF-Token: {{csrf}}

{ "items": [{ "mediaId": "REPLACE_WITH_MEDIA_ID", "role": "PRIMARY" }] }

###
POST {{api}}/admin/catalog/products/{{productId}}/publish
X-CSRF-Token: {{csrf}}

### 24. Duplicate it. New SKU and slug, DRAFT, no stock and no sales history.
POST {{api}}/admin/catalog/products/{{productId}}/duplicate
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF-Token: {{csrf}}

{ "includeVariants": true, "includeMedia": true }

### 25. Export products as CSV (values starting with = + - @ are neutralised)
GET {{api}}/admin/catalog/export/PRODUCT?format=csv

### 26. Download an import template
GET {{api}}/admin/catalog/import/templates/PRODUCT

### 27. Dry-run import — validates, writes nothing
# @name dryRun
POST {{api}}/admin/catalog/import/PRODUCT
X-CSRF-Token: {{csrf}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=ClearWoodBoundary

--ClearWoodBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="dryRun"

true
--ClearWoodBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="files"; filename="products.csv"
Content-Type: text/csv

< ./products.csv
--ClearWoodBoundary--

###
@jobId = {{dryRun.response.body.data.id}}

### 28. Inspect the validation report (row + column + message per error)
GET {{api}}/admin/catalog/import/jobs/{{jobId}}

### 29. Commit it for real (re-attach the same file)
POST {{api}}/admin/catalog/import/jobs/{{jobId}}/commit
X-CSRF-Token: {{csrf}}
Idempotency-Key: demo-import-commit-0001
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=ClearWoodBoundary

--ClearWoodBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="files"; filename="products.csv"
Content-Type: text/csv

< ./products.csv
--ClearWoodBoundary--

### 30. Import history
GET {{api}}/admin/catalog/import/jobs?limit=10

### 31. Bulk deactivate, with a per-id result array
POST {{api}}/admin/catalog/bulk
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF-Token: {{csrf}}

{ "action": "DEACTIVATE", "ids": ["{{productId}}"] }

### 32. Price rules (stored and validated; the engine itself is Prompt 6)
GET {{api}}/admin/catalog/price-adjustments?limit=20

### 33. Overlapping rules that will fight each other once stacking exists
GET {{api}}/admin/catalog/price-adjustments/conflicts

### 34. Attribute guards: deleting a value that variants use returns 409 with the counts
DELETE {{api}}/admin/catalog/attribute-values/REPLACE_WITH_IN_USE_VALUE_ID
X-CSRF-Token: {{csrf}}

### 35. Brands and tax classes
GET {{api}}/admin/catalog/brands
###
GET {{api}}/admin/catalog/tax-classes

### 36. Delete the demo category with each strategy on throwaway nodes
DELETE {{api}}/admin/catalog/categories/{{categoryId}}?strategy=REASSIGN_CHILDREN
X-CSRF-Token: {{csrf}}

###
POST {{api}}/admin/catalog/categories/{{categoryId}}/restore
X-CSRF-Token: {{csrf}}

###
DELETE {{api}}/admin/catalog/categories/{{categoryId}}?strategy=CASCADE_SOFT
X-CSRF-Token: {{csrf}}
